# build 119: the light pass's surface lists sorted without a call per
# comparison. structure_render_dynamic_triangles_from_indices sorts each
# list of surface indices with qsort_4byte, which calls
# compare_surface_indices through a pointer for every comparison: 9% of
# d20's drawing instructions (qsort_4byte 6.5%, the comparison 2.5%;
# hotlines119). psp_sort_surface_indices is the same algorithm (the same
# pivots, partitions and short sort, so the same swaps) with the comparison
# written in, and returns at once when the list is already in order. Values
# alone are sorted, so the list comes out the same. Then (the same build)
# a list with no index twice is put in order through a bit per surface
# instead (psp_order_surface_indices_by_bits): ~80,000 instructions a list
# on d20 become a few thousand. "surfaceqsort": as before;
# "surfacesortcheck": both, the results compared
FIXES_119 = {}
# build 119: the vertical blank thread above the game thread. The port's
# 60 Hz thread (d3d8_gl.c) counts the vertical blanks the game paces its
# clock by (main_update_time: a frame's game time is the blanks since the
# last, at most a fifteenth of a second). At priority 0x3c, below the game
# thread's 0x20, it only ran when the game thread waited, then counted the
# blanks it had missed all at once: one frame saw one blank, the next seven,
# and the cap threw the rest away. On the PSP-1000 (b118 test 4) b40 ran
# 1.43 ticks a frame at 16 fps where its frames' lengths give 1.8: the game
# ran at 77% of real time. At 0x1e it wakes on time (60 short wakes a
