# ---------- FIXES_OBSRAY: two rays of the obstacle-avoidance pill test reused
# (lever OBSRAY). A pill test (path_test_pill2d) casts six 2d rays across the
# pathfinding surfaces. Two of them repeat a call it has already made, with
# the same inputs: the right side's ray across the pill is the left side's
# call again (both pass the same perpendicular, not its negation; the engine's
# own behaviour, kept), and the last ray, which finds the surface at the
# result's distance, is the first ray again whenever no test shortened that
# distance. structure_test_ray2d reads only its arguments, the structure's
# tags and the breakable surfaces' flags, none of which a pill test changes,
# and writes every field of its result, so the earlier answer is the one the
# repeat would give: exact. An actor's think can make 100+ steps of this
# search, each with a pill test per step and per disc it floods, so the repeats
# are up to a third of the search's rays. "obsrayreuse" (on; obsrayreuseoff):
# the repeats reused
