# ---------- FIXES_TICKCACHE (lever GETTICKCACHE, keep word "tickcache", off by
# default): GetTickCount from a counter the vertical blank thread refreshes.
# The engine reads system_milliseconds -> GetTickCount ~72 times a tick (b30;
# syscall2 42350929915, syscall3 42357263684), each a system call
# (sceKernelGetSystemTimeWide) and a software 64-bit divide; the input's held
# buttons take 52 of them, keyboard and UI the rest. Windows' GetTickCount
# itself ticks every 10-16 ms, so a counter refreshed at each vertical blank
# (16.7 ms) keeps the original's resolution. main.c's frame timing reads the
# clock live (psp_milliseconds_live), as the game paces its ticks by it. The
