# ---------- FIXES_SPEECHPAD: the two AI dialogue callers zero their speech item (a fix, always on)
# unit_speak copies its caller's unit_speech_item whole into unit.speech
# (current or queued), pad bytes and all. Two callers build theirs on the stack
# field by field and never zero it: ai_communication.c's reply (the item at the
# pin's :4895, which also leaves ai.look_data unset) and the chosen possibility
# (:7138, whose ai part is a whole copy of ai_packet, itself set field by field
# from :7089). So unit.speech's pads (+0x350 current.ai's byte after
# updated_dialogue_timers, +0x35c the two after current.ai.information_type,
# +0x374 queued's word pad; row piece5dump_fields_named) carried whatever the
# stack held, which moves with what ran before, and the sleepers' checksum sums
# them whole (the lead 2026-11-25 18:3x (1): zeroed at the two callers, in
# both builds). Each item, and ai_packet, is zeroed at its first write; every
# named field is then set as before, so play reads the same values. A
# determinism fix, not a lever: always on, no keep word. Safe in every role
FIXES_SPEECHPAD = {}
